menu "MAO perception"

    config MAO_PERCEPT_NEAR_MM
        int "Proximity: 'near' distance through the window (mm)"
        range 50 800
        default 200
        help
            Something closer than this (two readings in a row) is
            APPROACH_NEAR; it has to move 50 % further away again before it
            counts as gone (hysteresis). VERIFY AT BRING-UP through the
            cover window: the window border adds crosstalk.

    config MAO_PERCEPT_QUIET_ROOM_S
        int "Quiet room after this many seconds of quiet"
        range 10 3600
        default 120

    config MAO_PERCEPT_DARK_ROOM_S
        int "Dark room after this many seconds of darkness"
        range 5 600
        default 20

    config MAO_PERCEPT_LONG_ABSENCE_MIN
        int "Long absence: minutes without anyone around"
        range 5 10080
        default 120
        help
            When someone comes back after at least this long (counting
            deep sleep), MAO perceives LONG_ABSENCE before anything else.

    config MAO_PERCEPT_IMU_Z_DOWN
        bool "IMU +Z points down when MAO rests on its base"
        default n
        help
            The LSM6DSOX sits on the face side of the A0, so its +Z axis
            should point up out of the face when MAO rests on its base.
            VERIFY AT BRING-UP with "mao sense" (accel z = +1 g at rest);
            enable this if it reads -1 g.

    config MAO_PERCEPT_LOG
        bool "Log every percept"
        default y
        help
            One INFO line per percept (release builds log WARN and above
            only, so this costs nothing there). "mao percept log off"
            silences it at run time.

endmenu
